  "title": "ISUP tap with proper message",
  "description": "The current ISUP tap handler is hardcoded to generate messages from the\ndefault ISUP `value_string_ext`, regardless of what variant is in use.\nIn addition, it doesn't handle messages that aren't in the\n`value_string_ext`.\n\nThis change store the ISUP variant in the tap record, and uses it to\ngenerate the appropriate message for the variant in use. In addition, it\nfollows behaviour elsewhere in the dissector and labels unknown messages\nas \"reserved\".",
